   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>State Representative (2013-present), Transportation Committee Chair; Tacoma City Councilmember (2006-2012)</span></p><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><p>Director, Washington State University Energy Program; Former Energy Services Manager, Tacoma Power;&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Board Member, Puget Sound Regional Council Economic Development District and Transportation Policy Board; Board Member, Pierce Transit and Sound Transit; Vice-Chair, Puget Sound Clean Air Agency; Chair, Tacoma Public Utility Board; Board Member, Tacoma-Pierce County Health Department</span></p><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/>B.A. Political Science, University of Washington; Master's in Public Administration, University of Puget Sound<br /><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/>Board Member, Boys and Girls Club of South Puget Sound; Board President, Tacoma-Pierce County Big Brothers/Big Sisters; Rotary 8<br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><span></span>\r\n<p><span>It&rsquo;s an honor to serve you and your family, delivering on priorities like affordable and emergency housing, expanding access to behavioral health, and improving public safety. As House Transportation Chair, I help create jobs and build the roads, bridges, ferries, and pedestrian infrastructure we need to keep our communities and commutes safe</span><span>.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span>But there is more to be done. With your vote, I&rsquo;ll continue to advocate for affordable childcare, K-12 excellence, higher education access, and workforce training. I&rsquo;m proud of my 100% pro-choice and LGBTQ rights voting record.&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Endorsed: State Labor Council, Building Trades, WA Conservation Action, Firefighters, Nurses, Teachers.</span></p>\r\n<div><span><br />\r\n</span></div><br/><br/>",
